                        <div class="faq-item">
                            <button class="faq-question" onclick="toggleFAQ(this)">
                                <span class="faq-q-icon"><i class="fas fa-question"></i></span>
                                <span class="faq-q-text">How do I care for solid wood furniture?</span>
                                <span class="faq-chevron"><i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i></span>
                            </button>
                            <div class="faq-answer">
                                <div class="faq-answer-inner">
                                    <p>Solid wood furniture is beautiful and durable — with the right care, it will last
                                        for generations. Here are our essential care tips:</p>
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>Dust with a soft, dry or slightly damp microfibre cloth weekly</li>
                                        <li>Avoid placing directly in sunlight or near AC vents — temperature
                                            fluctuations cause cracking</li>
                                        <li>Use coasters, placemats and tablecloths to protect surfaces from heat and
                                            moisture</li>
                                        <li>Apply teak or wood oil once every 6–12 months to maintain lustre</li>
                                        <li>Clean spills immediately with a dry cloth — never let liquid sit</li>
                                        <li>Avoid chemical cleaners, bleach or furniture polish containing silicone</li>
                                    </ul>
                                    <div class="answer-highlight"><i class="fas fa-box"></i> A free care kit including
                                        wood oil and microfibre cloth is included with every solid wood purchase.</div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

